{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDI0L1ByaW50JTIwSXQlMjBCbGFjayUyMCUyODIwMjQlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Print It Black","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/zophRgfZ0158E3ccW0XTLQSBLzj.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ai0o2Yj99gBVt4yecGz0brp4jAW.jpg","description":"After the Robb Elementary school shooting in Texas, local Uvalde Leader-News journalists are left to report on the fallout – and on one of their staff members. Reporter Kimberly Rubio rises to national prominence as an advocate for gun reform after her ten-year-old daughter, Lexi, is killed in the shooting. Through the journalists’ reporting, we witness the social fabric of this small Texas town unravel as Kimberly and other victims’ families search for accountability from law enforcement and local leaders. The documentary also shines a light on the critical role of community journalism, at a time when local newspapers are folding rapidly across the country.\n\nRated NR · Released 28 Apr 2024 · United States of America · Language: English · 86 min\nStudio: ABC News\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2024","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.0","imdb_id":"tt32265065","moviedb_id":1274970,"tmdbId":1274970,"runtime":"86 min","cast":["Pete Luna","Craig Garnett","Beto O'Rourke","Sheila Jackson Lee","Meghann Garcia","Melissa Federspill","Julye Keeble","Kimberly Mata-Rubio"],"director":["Tomas Navia"],"released":"2024-04-28T00:00:00.000Z","country":"United States of America","language":"English","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Tomas Navia","character":"Director"},{"name":"Pete Luna","character":"Self"},{"name":"Craig Garnett","character":"Self"},{"name":"Beto O'Rourke","character":"Self","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/9lE8qep5EwgGrJag99wqW8DIGqo.jpg"},{"name":"Sheila Jackson Lee","character":"Self"},{"name":"Meghann Garcia","character":"Self"},{"name":"Melissa Federspill","character":"Self"},{"name